+## Checkbox State Tracking (the plan file is the durable progress log)
+
+Every actionable step uses a `- [ ]` checkbox. These are not cosmetic — they encode persistent execution state:
+
+- `- [ ]` = pending. Must still be done.
+- `- [x]` = completed. Verified passing. Do NOT redo.
+
+**Contract for plan authors:**
+- Every step that an executor must perform gets its own `- [ ]` checkbox on a line by itself, in the form `- [ ] **Step N: <imperative description>**`. Sub-bullets, code blocks, and explanatory prose hang under the step but do not get their own checkboxes.
+- Tasks themselves (the `### Task N: ...` headings) are NOT checkboxed — task completion is implied by all steps inside being `- [x]`.
+- Header notes outside any task (Goal, Architecture, Execution Strategy, Agent Assignments) never get checkboxes.
+- Do not author a plan with any pre-checked `- [x]` boxes. Executors interpret them as "skip this".
+
+**Contract for executors** (see executing-plans / subagent-driven-development for the full procedure):
+- On load, scan for `- [x]` and skip those steps.
+- On step verify, immediately edit the plan file to flip `- [ ]` → `- [x]` for that exact line. Commit periodically — the file is the cross-session resume point.
+
